  IX. KEY FINDING: THE (1,2) PEAK
  --------------------------------------------------

  Tournaments at (hw0=1, hw1=2): 96
  H values: [11, 13, 19, 23, 25, 27, 29, 31, 33, 37, 41, 43, 45]
  c3 values: [4, 5, 6, 7, 8]

  Tournaments at (hw0=4, hw1=3): 8
  H values: [1, 9, 17, 23, 33, 41]
  c3 values: [0, 3, 4, 6, 8]

  At (hw0=4, hw1=3): all skip-2 and skip-3 forward.
  Path forward + skip-2 forward + skip-3 forward means:
  i->j for j-i in {1,2,3}. So vertex i dominates i+1, i+2, i+3.
  This ALMOST determines the tournament (only skip-4 and skip-5 free).
  Only 2^2 * 2^1 = 8 free bits remain.
  Count: 8 (should be 2^3 = 8)

  At (hw0=1, hw1=2): 1 of 4 skip-2 forward, 2 of 3 skip-3 forward.
  'Almost backward' on short range + 'mostly forward' on medium range
  = maximum structural tension = maximum H.

